🌍 TIMEZONE-AWARE REMINDER TIMING
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

CRITICAL: Always send reminders in CUSTOMER'S TIMEZONE, not business timezone.

PROBLEM: Business sends all reminders at fixed UTC time
"Reminder at 14:00 UTC"
- NY customer (EDT): 10:00am ✅ Good time
- Madrid customer (CEST): 4:00pm ✅ Good time
- Tokyo customer (JST): 11:00pm ❌ Too late!

SOLUTION: Calculate reminder time in customer's timezone first

Algorithm:
1. Get booking time (stored as UTC)
   Example: Wed 22, 14:00 UTC
2. Get customer timezone
   Example: America/New_York (EDT = UTC-4)
3. Calculate 24h and 1h before in customer's timezone
   24h before: Tue 21, 14:00 UTC = 10:00am EDT
   1h before: Wed 22, 13:00 UTC = 09:00am EDT
4. Convert reminder times TO UTC (for scheduler)
   24h reminder: Schedule for Tue 21, 14:00 UTC
   1h reminder: Schedule for Wed 22, 13:00 UTC
5. When scheduler fires at UTC time, convert back to customer TZ for display
   Message: "¡En 1 hora! Tu consulta a las 10:00am EDT"

Example with Multiple Timezones:

Same Booking Time (stored as UTC): 14:00 UTC on Oct 22

Customer 1 (NY, EDT = UTC-4):
- Booking local time: 10:00am Wednesday
- 24h reminder sent: Tue 10:00am EDT (= 14:00 UTC)
- 1h reminder sent: Wed 09:00am EDT (= 13:00 UTC)

Customer 2 (Madrid, CEST = UTC+2):
- Booking local time: 4:00pm Wednesday
- 24h reminder sent: Tue 4:00pm CEST (= 14:00 UTC)
- 1h reminder sent: Wed 03:00pm CEST (= 13:00 UTC)

Customer 3 (Tokyo, JST = UTC+9):
- Booking local time: 11:00pm Wednesday
- 24h reminder sent: Tue 11:00pm JST (= 14:00 UTC)
- 1h reminder sent: Wed 10:00pm JST (= 13:00 UTC)

All sent at same UTC times, but arrive in each customer's comfortable hours! ✅

