🎯 TIER-BASED REMINDER PERSONALIZATION
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

TIER 1 (NEW CUSTOMERS):
├─ Strategy: CONSERVATIVE (don't overwhelm)
├─ 24h reminder: Email only (safe, no channel preference known)
├─ 1h reminder: Email only (consistent)
├─ 15m reminder: None (too aggressive for new)
├─ No-show follow-up: Friendly, no penalty
└─ Message tone: Helpful, reassuring ("we're here to help")

Example Email Tone:
"Hola! Solo te recordamos que mañana tienes tu consulta.
Si tienes dudas, ¡escríbeme! Estoy aquí para ayudarte."

TIER 2 (RECURRING CUSTOMERS):
├─ Strategy: BALANCED (they know the drill)
├─ 24h reminder: Email + SMS (more engagement)
├─ 1h reminder: Email + SMS (critical reminder)
├─ 15m reminder: SMS only (optional)
├─ No-show follow-up: Slight concern ("hey, everything ok?")
└─ Message tone: Friendly, familiar ("hey, just confirming...")

Example SMS Tone:
"¡Hola de nuevo! Mañana a las 10:00am. Nos vemos online 😊"

TIER 3 (POWER CUSTOMERS):
├─ Strategy: AGGRESSIVE (they want efficiency)
├─ 24h reminder: SMS + Push only (no email clutter)
├─ 1h reminder: SMS + Push (they're busy)
├─ 15m reminder: Push only (heads up)
├─ No-show follow-up: Quick escalation (deposit required?)
└─ Message tone: Concise, professional ("confirmed: tomorrow 10am")

Example SMS Tone:
"Confirmed: Tomorrow 10am EDT. Link: [SHORT]. Questions? Call."

TIER 4 (AT-RISK CUSTOMERS):
├─ Strategy: MINIMAL (reduce friction, build trust)
├─ 24h reminder: Email only (least intrusive)
├─ 1h reminder: Email only (respect their space)
├─ 15m reminder: None (too much)
├─ No-show follow-up: PHONE CALL (personal touch)
└─ Message tone: Warm, personal ("we'd love to see you")

Example Email Tone:
"Hola! Espero que todo esté bien. Solo confirmando que mañana...
Si hay algún problema, no dudes en llamarme personalmente."

